drm/amdgpu/gfx11: disallow gfxoff around GPU reset (hand-adapted)

Original idea and Signed-off-by from Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>,
posted 2026-07-06 as [PATCH 3/7] on the amd-gfx list (still under review as of
2026-09-16 -- Lijo Lazar requested the gfxoff-ctrl calls be consolidated into
shared reset-helper begin/end logic rather than scattered per reset
function). Thread: https://ratatoskr.run/amd-gfx/2026/07/17221331/t

Deucher's original commit message, unchanged:

  If gfx is hung, we shouldn't need this since gfx won't be powered down,
  but we could potentially have a case where a queue can be preempted, but
  due logic errors in the commands, the fence never signals. GFX could
  potentially go into the off state. Protect against that.

The original diff no longer applies: gfx_v11_0_reset_kgq()/reset_kcq() have
since been refactored (amdgpu_gfx_mes_reset_queue -> renamed
amdgpu_mes_reset_legacy_queue, plus a new pipe-reset fallback path added)
independently of this fix. Confirmed by reading nixpkgs-unstable's actual
7.2.5 source that neither function -- nor amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_begin/end,
nor amdgpu_mes_reset_legacy_queue itself -- calls amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl()
anywhere, so the race Deucher describes is still open in current code. This
hand-adapts the same fix (disable gfxoff for the duration of the reset
attempt including any pipe-reset fallback, goto-based cleanup so it's always
re-enabled on every exit path) onto the current function bodies, for both
reset_kgq and reset_kcq (the original patch only touched reset_kgq; reset_kcq
has the identical gap).

NOT reviewed by AMD -- written and tested locally against the exact "reset
via MES failed and try pipe reset" / "MES failed to respond" / failed GPU
reset hangs on Framework 16's 780M (gfx1103) iGPU. See systems/NOlaptop.nix
for the full trace history that led here.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c
@@ -6919,30 +6919,36 @@

 	amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_begin(ring, timedout_fence);

+	amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl(adev, false);
+
 	r = amdgpu_mes_reset_legacy_queue(ring->adev, ring, vmid, use_mmio, 0);
 	if (r) {

 		dev_warn(adev->dev, "reset via MES failed and try pipe reset %d\n", r);
 		r = gfx_v11_reset_gfx_pipe(ring);
 		if (r)
-			return r;
+			goto fail;
 	}

 	if (use_mmio) {
 		r = gfx_v11_0_kgq_init_queue(ring, true);
 		if (r) {
 			dev_err(adev->dev, "failed to init kgq\n");
-			return r;
+			goto fail;
 		}

 		r = amdgpu_mes_map_legacy_queue(adev, ring, 0);
 		if (r) {
 			dev_err(adev->dev, "failed to remap kgq\n");
-			return r;
+			goto fail;
 		}
 	}

-	return amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, timedout_fence);
+	r = amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, timedout_fence);
+
+fail:
+	amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl(adev, true);
+	return r;
 }

 static int gfx_v11_0_reset_compute_pipe(struct amdgpu_ring *ring)
@@ -7084,26 +7090,32 @@

 	amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_begin(ring, timedout_fence);

+	amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl(adev, false);
+
 	r = amdgpu_mes_reset_legacy_queue(ring->adev, ring, vmid, true, 0);
 	if (r) {
 		dev_warn(adev->dev, "fail(%d) to reset kcq and try pipe reset\n", r);
 		r = gfx_v11_0_reset_compute_pipe(ring);
 		if (r)
-			return r;
+			goto fail;
 	}

 	r = gfx_v11_0_kcq_init_queue(ring, true);
 	if (r) {
 		dev_err(adev->dev, "fail to init kcq\n");
-		return r;
+		goto fail;
 	}
 	r = amdgpu_mes_map_legacy_queue(adev, ring, 0);
 	if (r) {
 		dev_err(adev->dev, "failed to remap kcq\n");
-		return r;
+		goto fail;
 	}

-	return amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, timedout_fence);
+	r = amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, timedout_fence);
+
+fail:
+	amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl(adev, true);
+	return r;
 }

 static void gfx_v11_ip_print(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block, struct drm_printer *p)
